WEBVTT

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.500
They got away...

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.910
Relax, Vestulse.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.180
We have another use for them.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.540
This impacts nothing.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:31.930
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:41.930
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:52.310
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:00:52.310 --> 00:01:02.310
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:12.490
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:23.010
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:33.010
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:43.700
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.220
Wh-What was that?

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.160
I don't know.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.790
But it saved us...

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.330
Yeah.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.670
But why would light just--

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:24.160
Emilio!

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.200
Alicia! Pascal!

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.850
How dare you leave like that!

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.080
Well, uh...

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.810
What were you thinking?!

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:39.220
How'd you like my fancy incendiary?

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:46.060
When heat is applied to a certain metal, it emits a flame much brighter than your usual wood.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.500
But my version uses a special catalyst mixed with

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:53.940
the metal to speed up the reaction and produces a much greater--

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.510
How about you fill us in on the details another time?

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:03.110
No one appreciates the depth of my knowledge...

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:06.380
Pascal, Alicia... What are you doing here?

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:08.020
What kind of attitude is that?

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:12.890
When someone lands in trouble, their friends will come to help.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:17.190
Especially when they get involved with an unsavory crowd...

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:31.640
"6: Determination"

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.910
What happened to the others?

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.250
They split up and went off on their own.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.550
Many of them sustained injuries.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:43.490
So, who do we have here?

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.790
You don't seem like a typical old-timer.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:52.260
I'm nothing more than an old geezer who enjoys dabbling in science.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:56.070
I-Is it just me, or does it feel a little tense here?

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.800
Demetrio, listen!

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.800
These two are my friends.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.240
They didn't come to fight!

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.970
Aren't all friends of yours associates of the king?

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.610
Emilio...

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.450
Let's go.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:17.950
Huh? Hey!

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:23.090
Right. If we dawdle around here, we'll run into those pests again.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.360
Hey! Wait for me!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.630
Shun! Wait up!

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.020
We'll stop in that town for the night.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.610
We've got to go over our plans for the future.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.550
See you later!

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:54.610
Uh, wait!

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.370
Who are those people anyway?

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:19.750
I'm sure you've already figured it out.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:25.020
Then they must be a band of people aiming to overthrow the king...

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.160
Emilio...

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:33.250
So it's true that you tried to assassinate the king?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.940
And that's the reason you were put in the dungeons...

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:47.840
I knew you despised the man, but I didn't think you'd ever try to kill your father.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:48.940
He's not my father!

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.580
But he raised you!

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.780
I'll be the one to bring down Delzaine.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:57.290
That's why I partnered with these revolutionaries.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.560
I'll use whoever and whatever it takes...

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.620
...if it means avenging my father.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.260
Emilio...

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.860
Do we know if what you believe is true?

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:13.360
Was it really Delzaine who killed your father, the former king?

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.800
That's what I've heard...

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.300
You've only heard?

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:21.210
That by itself is insufficient proof.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.370
You don't even know if that really happened!

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:31.220
Even supposing he killed the previous king, you don't know the reason why.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:34.090
Everything is done for a reason.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:36.630
He just wanted the throne for himself!

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:39.560
He killed my father to further his own greed!

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.930
That is merely an assumption.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:43.420
There is no proof...

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:48.630
Have you even asked Delzaine to tell you the truth?

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:51.570
You haven't...

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:57.240
Before taking the easy path of revenge, you should first find out the truth.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.760
I wonder what those two are talking about?

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.830
I'm sure Pascal's just mad at him.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.930
Emilio deserves to get one of his three-hour lectures.

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:22.600
What about you, Shun?
Why didn't you try to stop him?

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.670
What does it matter?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:29.310
Those people trying to sabotage the government are dangerous!

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:32.050
Emilio shouldn't be with them...

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:35.780
Wait a second, sabotage the government?

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:39.220
That's what it means to bring down the king!

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:44.130
Demetrio and the others aren't like that... probably.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:48.960
In any case, why didn't he even ask me to come along?

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:51.130
Huh? Is that all?

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:54.500
It sounds like you're just mad that he left you behind.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.670
You idiot!

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.240
What was that about?

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:08.880
Now Shun's saying it, too...

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:14.360
Emilio...

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:26.770
Emilio!

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:30.910
Alicia!

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:32.840
Did you sneak inside the castle again?

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:36.380
Yeah! I like exploring around in here!

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:37.950
But they'll get mad at you.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.280
It's okay. They've got to find me first.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:45.390
Alicia? You're not supposed to be inside the castle!

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:47.910
Come here at once, Alicia!

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:55.630
Lord Emilio? Have you seen Alicia anywhere?

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.570
Yeah. I saw her running that way.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:00.140
Thank you very much.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:01.570
Alicia!

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.110
Sorry about that.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:16.590
It's okay... But what's so fun about the castle?

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:20.590
Well, I always go and play around in the forest...

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:22.960
...but it's boring doing that every day.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:28.400
It is? In my case,
I'm getting bored of the castle...

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.890
The forest, huh? I'd like to go there sometime...

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:36.340
Then I'll take you the next time I go!

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:41.240
There's big boars and strange mushrooms all over the forest!

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:43.010
It's really fun!

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:44.450
Yeah?

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.590
Emilio...

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.500
Emilio...

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:29.520
I searched all over the city but the Royal Guard has no influence here.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.360
I guess we won't have to worry then.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:33.860
Though we can't stay here for long.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.700
So, what do you plan to do now?

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.330
First we need to gather some numbers.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:41.740
Many of our comrades were lost.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:46.980
The recent battle dealt us a severe blow.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:52.010
What will you do about Emilio and Shun?

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:54.720
We'll keep them with us for the time being.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:57.990
That prince still may prove useful.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.020
Besides...

00:10:59.020 --> 00:10:59.860
Besides?

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:06.030
It might have taken both of them, but Emilio and Shun stood up against one of the Truculent.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:09.000
It's not like they're entirely useless.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.570
And the other two?

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.170
We'll keep an eye on them.

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:15.670
I'm asking you if you've seen four weird people!

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:17.510
I'm trying to close shop here!

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:20.940
But have you seen a guy with a feather sticking out of his hat?

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.880
Or this guy who kinda looks like a girl, or--

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:25.280
No, I haven't.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:26.750
Don't worry about him.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.350
You can let him through.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.900
Did you come alone? What about the others?

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:50.370
Emilio and Pascal are having some sort of argument.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.870
And Alicia's just acting angry.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.540
They're all in a bad mood so I'd rather not be there.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:59.450
Oh. Pascal and Alicia are the other two that showed up today.

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:02.650
Who are those two anyway?

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:05.720
They're both Emilio's old friends.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:11.430
Pascal said he used to be in the Royal Laboratory or something.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:12.890
The Royal Laboratory?

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:16.900
More importantly, I need to get to Babylon as fast as possible!

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.930
Babylon, eh?

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:21.640
I'll be able to get to the surface from there.

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:26.170
I'm pretty sure I return because Eljuia saw it in my future.

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:28.280
But your future...

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:32.950
I just want to get home, not fight or help Emilio get revenge.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:35.650
The road to Babylon is perilous.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:41.120
Not only do you have to cross a large body of water...

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:44.130
...you must pass through lands occupied by a vicious bunch.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.800
One wrong move and you die.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.930
What? Die?

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:50.420
Does that scare you?

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:55.670
No. I still want to get back to the surface.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.040
I'm worried about my mother.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:01.310
My father's never around, so someone's got to be there for her.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:06.150
Babylon is our destination as well.

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.780
Delzaine seems to be headed that way.

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:11.950
He'll have less protection there than in the castle.

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:13.960
It's a good chance for us to get him.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.790
Don't expect us to babysit you the entire time.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:19.800
It's survival of the fittest out there.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:22.630
I can protect myself just fine.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.030
That's good to hear.

00:13:48.690 --> 00:13:50.530
There you are!

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:52.030
I've been looking for you.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:53.430
Shun?

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:56.100
Did Pascal give you a good scolding?

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.700
For going off on your own?

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:02.500
Pascal... He knows nothing.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.540
You're the one who knows nothing.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.110
What?!

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:10.010
Pascal is just worried about you.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:12.210
Otherwise he wouldn't have come here.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:17.420
Anyhow, it's late, so let's get some rest.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:21.050
Demetrio and the others are already setting up the tents.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:30.300
You're still here? Go home, Alicia.

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:33.600
Don't get involved in something that has nothing to do with you.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:36.300
It does involve me!

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:37.940
It's your call then.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.460
I don't need you to tell me!

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.470
By the way, where's Pascal?

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:49.550
Check it out! It's my mini hand-held flamethrower!

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:50.720
Amazing!

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.250
That's so useful!

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:55.420
How does this contraption work?

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:58.590
Pascal? He's already with the others...

00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:01.100
Oh, it's you two.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:03.300
He's pretty cool for a grandpa!

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.970
Grandpa?!

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:08.460
He sure is getting along with everybody...

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:20.650
You two go scout the area.

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.950
Felix needs your help.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:24.950
--Hey!
--Let me go!

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:26.020
It's patrol time.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:27.620
Ow! Hey!

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:30.960
Should we start preparing for tomorrow?

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:32.290
Sure.

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.630
Hey...

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:37.800
Your name was Alicia, right?

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:38.970
Um...

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:40.700
I'm Louise.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:43.710
Just one of the bad guys in this evil gang.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:46.110
Louise, was it?

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:50.180
So, do you plan on coming along with us?

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:54.120
Yeah. If Emilio is going, I'm coming, too.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.620
Hmm?

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:56.990
What?

00:15:56.990 --> 00:16:01.520
I'm sick of being the only girl in this crew.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:06.330
Though, with one of them it's hard to tell if he's a girl or guy...

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:09.360
But being surrounded by guys is getting on my nerves!

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:15.200
So it would be great to have another girl like you with us!

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:20.310
Right... But aren't you all trying to overthrow the kingdom?

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:21.680
We sure are.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:25.580
Then why does everyone seem so cheerful?

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:31.690
Did you think we'd be a bit more wicked and barbaric?

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:33.890
Yeah...

00:16:33.890 --> 00:16:38.430
There isn't much difference between us and you.

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:41.990
We just grew up under different circumstances.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:49.100
By the way, Alicia... Emilio is the heir apparent to Delzaine, correct?

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:51.870
Yeah, he is...

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:56.280
Then who is this Shun who's always fighting with him?

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.880
I don't really know either.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:03.520
He says he's from the surface, but he can use a Warp Relic...

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:04.950
Hmm...

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:07.290
Louise!

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:09.620
Could you give me a hand?

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:13.030
Fine, fine! Oh well...

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:16.470
Got it, Alicia? Let's get along, you and I.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.230
What do you need?

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:24.110
We're leaving tomorrow morning, so we need to gather everything we're bringing along.

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:25.640
Got it!

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:27.070
What a weird person...

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:34.050
Ah, what a bummer.

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:39.290
Emilio's in a bad mood as always, and Felix barely talks.

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:42.420
I'm not even sure what to say.

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:46.900
Here goes nothing.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:51.920
Hey, Felix? Why are you trying to defeat the king anyhow?

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:56.770
You guys barely survived back there.

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:58.300
I'd like to know as well.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.970
Injustice runs rampant in Endora.

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:11.290
Those born in poverty and those persecuted for their race...

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:16.160
Even if they've done no wrong, they live under constant torment and cruelty.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:19.630
Many of us and our supporters are among them.

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:23.330
Demetrio is trying to change the world.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:26.330
I think he's the only one who can.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.840
That's why I fight at his side.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:31.540
Change the world...

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:32.940
I see...

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:35.180
We're splitting up to cover ground.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:38.650
You two go in that direction.
I'm going this way.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:39.810
Uh...

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:41.810
He just left us...

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:41.580
Taking measurements this late at night?

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:44.210
It's a bad habit of mine.

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:46.750
It's not always without perks.

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:51.020
So, you formerly belonged to the Royal Laboratory?

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:53.050
That was way in the past.

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:56.560
What is Delzaine trying to accomplish?

00:19:56.560 --> 00:20:00.300
Who knows. Not even I have a clue...

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.600
I can tell you're not lying.

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:06.730
I'd like to know what he's after more than anyone.

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:10.740
He won't share his intentions with anyone else...

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:13.800
Not even with his own son... Emilio.

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:19.710
That spoiled prince still has some growing to do.

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:22.410
He's got a ways to go before being fit to be a king.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:29.790
As I feared, the Warp Particles are decreasing.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.590
Does the restoration of Babel have anything to do with it?

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:45.230
All right! Everyone get ready to leave!

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:01.620
Nothing will stop me from getting back to the surface!

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.890
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:09.660
<i>Took a long way to get here</i>

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:13.640
<i>Had to go around and around</i>

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:17.770
<i>But every single road I've taken</i>

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:21.640
<i>Made me who I am today</i>

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:28.610
<i>go my way go my way</i>

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:40.060
<i>The world will show you there's tomorrow</i>

00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:48.630
<i>Look up to the blue sky and you will see</i>

00:21:49.470 --> 00:21:57.510
<i>I try to be better than who I was yesterday</i>

00:21:57.510 --> 00:22:04.690
<i>So I can see you with a smile on my face today</i>

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:09.920
<i>Now what should we get into today?</i>

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:18.570
<i>The scent of summer arouses my heart</i>

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:23.710
<i>And I can't seem to find the right words to tell you</i>

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:28.170
<i>That I love you just the way you are</i>

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:39.920
"Episode 7: Girl"

00:22:37.790 --> 00:22:39.720
